 ### [Voxel Color Mapping](2970-voxel-color-mapping.md)
-Voxel Color Mapping is a technique that maps scalar data values to integer indices for direct lookup in a color table, translating numerical volume data into visual appearance. It serves as the final step in the classification pipeline, distinct from complex transfer functions that map multiple attributes to opacity and color; instead, it performs a direct lookup based on a normalized input, often used for maximum intensity projection or surface visualization where opacity is fixed or handled separately. Unlike [Parametric Function Generation](5349-parametric-function-generation.md) which computes colors via continuous functions, this method relies on discrete table indexing.
