 ### Hounsfield Scale Color Mapping
-A method to assign color values to voxels based on attenuation coefficients (e.g., from CT scans) using the Hounsfield scale [S10, unofficial]. The Hounsfield value is calculated as $HU = \frac{\mu_{tissue} - \mu_{water}}{\mu_{water}} \times 1000$ [S10, unofficial]. Water has a HU value of 0, air -1000, and bone 500–1500 [S10, unofficial]. Implemented as a LUT where a color value is read out for a given HU value [S10, unofficial].
